# Unbound declarations

<!-- Generated by lithon-codegen from unbound.json: edit that, then rerun `lithon-codegen toy spec`. -->

hs-bindgen does not bind these declarations of the Toy 1.0 headers. [`unbound.json`](unbound.json) gives each one a disposition, and `spec` and `generate` fail on a skip without one and on a disposition for a name that is bound now.

| Disposition | Skips |
| ----------- | ----: |
| `shim`      |     2 |
| `constant`  |     1 |
| `wontfix`   |     3 |
| `upstream`  |     2 |

- `shim`: a lithon-authored C shim binds it instead.
- `constant`: lithon binds its value as a typed constant (`constants.json`).
- `wontfix`: it stays unbound on purpose.
- `upstream`: it waits on an hs-bindgen fix.

## `shim` (2)

Variadic; a C shim binds a fixed-arity twin.

- `toy_other_log` (toy_other.h:4): variadic
- `toy_log` (toy_skip.h:7): variadic

## `constant` (1)

A cast to a typedef; the typed constant carries the value.

- `macro TOY_MAX_SIZE` (toy_skip.h:6): macro-typecheck: `Failed to typecheck macro: Constraints are inconsistent: - 1: 'Sub Type (IntLike (CIntegralType (IntLike (Int Signed))))'`

## `upstream` (2)

A function shadowed by a same-name macro; hs-bindgen drops both.

Issue: <https://github.com/well-typed/hs-bindgen/issues/2097>

- `macro toy_memcpy` (toy_skip.h:11): conflict with a same-name declaration (toy_skip.h:11, toy_skip.h:12)
- `toy_memcpy` (toy_skip.h:11): conflict with a same-name declaration (toy_skip.h:11, toy_skip.h:12)

## `wontfix` (3)

No Haskell FFI type for long double; the hidden type is never bound.

- `toy_wide` (toy_skip.h:8): parse: `Unsupported floating-point type long double`
- `toy_wide_get` (toy_skip.h:9): parse: `Parse failure of underlying type of typedef 'toy_wide': Unsupported floating-point type long double`
- `toy_hidden_get` (toy_skip.h:10): needs `toy_hidden` (not selected), `struct toy_hidden` (not selected)

## Blocking dependencies outside the bound headers

Declarations the skips above need that no bound header declares, with how many skips each blocks.

- `struct toy_hidden` (toy_hidden.h:3): not selected; blocks 1
- `toy_hidden` (toy_hidden.h:3): not selected; blocks 1

